Slide-by-slide:
1. Title - ALRO: the company brain that keeps your team's promises.
2. Problem - decisions and promises are scattered across Slack, email and WhatsApp; nobody can find "what did we agree with Finlo?" in under 10 minutes.
3. Solution - ALRO ingests every channel, builds a timeline of facts and commitments, and answers with citations.
4. Demo screenshots - placeholder for now, need your latest UI.
5. How it works - connectors via Nango, Postgres + pgvector on Neon, cheap model screens, stronger model extracts. Keep it to one diagram.
6. Trust - row-level security mirrors source permissions; Google CASA assessment in progress.
7. Market - Indian SMB SaaS teams first, then global teams under 50 people.
8. Business model - $39/user/month, design partners free during the pilot.
9. Traction - three design partner calls done, Kirana Kart pilot under discussion, Finlo and Brightdesk in conversation.
10. Team - you and me (need a better photo of you than the Goa one).
11. Roadmap - Phase 1: Slack, Gmail, WhatsApp, CRM. Teams/Outlook later.
12. The ask - pre-seed round, amount TBD after we talk.

Open questions:
